<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bushati family</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1757–1831</span> · Also known as Bushatis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bushati family was an Albanian dynasty that ruled the Pashalik of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shkoder">Scutari</a> from Shkodër between 1757 and 1831. Taking advantage of Ottoman weakness, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehmed-pasha-bushati">Mehmed Pasha Bushati</a> and his son Kara Mahmud Pasha built an autonomous domain over northern Albania and neighbouring lands, while later members alternated between rebellion and service to the sultan. Their rule ended when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mustafa-pasha-bushati">Mustafa Pasha Bushati</a> surrendered to the grand <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/resid-mehmed-pasha">Reşid Mehmed Pasha</a> in 1831.</p></div>
